# Ceiling for the always-on rule set's estimated token cost, checked by
# scripts/rule-budget.py (make audit). A plain integer, nothing else.
#
# Copy to `.rule-budget` next to wherever rules/ actually resolves to — the
# rules repo's root for a separate SBW_RULES_DIR, or here for a
# self-contained checkout. Same idea as AGENTS.md sitting alongside rules/.
#
# 2000 is a starting point, not a measured one — this engine ships no rules
# of its own to calibrate against. Run `make audit` once you have a real
# rule set and adjust to what's actually there plus headroom, not the other
# way around.
2000
